   "text": "I read the molecule as a PROTAC-like compound with three parts: a pyrido[4,3-d]pyrimidine warhead, a pyrrolidine\u2013piperidine\u2013piperidine linker, and a glutarimide-substituted isoindolinone.\n\n**Warhead**\n- The core is a pyrido[4,3-d]pyrimidine.\n- C4 carries a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane attached through its N3, with the bridging NH free.\n- C8 carries F.\n- C7 carries a naphthalene attached through its C1. The naphthalene has OH at C3, an ethynyl at C8 and F at C7.\n- C2 carries an O\u2013CH2 group leading to the pyrrolidine.\n\n**Linker**\n- The pyrrolidine is N-methylated. Its C2 bears the CH2O group on a wedge, and its C4 bears an O on a hash.\n- That O connects to piperidin-4-yl. The piperidine N is linked by CH2 to the 4-position of a second piperidine.\n- The second piperidine N is bonded to the isoindolinone aryl ring.\n\n**Stereochemistry of the pyrrolidine (from the wedge and hash)**\n- C2 has N > CH2O > C3 > H, with H pointing away. N \u2192 CH2O \u2192 C3 runs counterclockwise, so C2 is S.\n- C4 has O > C5 > C3 > H, with H toward the viewer. O \u2192 C5 \u2192 C3 runs counterclockwise from the front, which reverses to clockwise, so C4 is R.\n- In the SMILES below, `[C@@H]` for C2 and `[C@@H]` for C4 give (2S,4R).\n\n**Isoindolinone**\n- The lactam carbonyl is at C1 and the CH2 at C3.\n- C4 carries F, C5 carries the piperidine N, and C7 carries a methyl.\n- The lactam N is attached to a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl (glutarimide) group.\n\nI used ring-closure label 8 for the glutarimide so it does not clash with the aromatic ring label 6 that is still open at that point.\n\nSMILES: C#Cc1c(F)ccc2cc(O)cc(c12)-c1ncc2c(N3CC4CCC(C3)N4)nc(OC[C@@H]5C[C@@H](OC6CCN(CC6)CC6CCN(CC6)c6cc(C)c7c(c6F)CN(C8CCC(=O)NC8=O)C7=O)CN5C)nc2c1F"
